<Base lang="en" title="Editorial Policy — eDistrict UP Seva" description="The eDistrict UP Seva editorial policy — what we publish, how information is checked, our corrections policy, and who writes this site." path="/en/editorial-policy/" altPath="/editorial-policy/" updated="27 November 2026" datePublished="2026-11-27" dateModified="2026-11-27">
  <div class="content-col">
    <h1 class="page-title">Editorial Policy</h1>

    <section class="box">
      <p><strong>eDistrict UP Seva is an independent, private information guide.</strong> It has no relationship, affiliation or endorsement from the Government of Uttar Pradesh, the eDistrict project, the National Informatics Centre (NIC), the eSathi portal, or CSC e-Governance. The only official portal of the Government of Uttar Pradesh is <strong>edistrict.up.gov.in</strong>.</p>

      <h2>What we publish</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Step-by-step application guides for Uttar Pradesh eDistrict / eSathi certificates (income, caste, domicile, birth, death, family-register copy, and others), in Hindi and English.</li>
        <li>How to check application status, download and verify a certificate, and avoid common mistakes that get applications rejected.</li>
        <li>Blog articles — such as a forms list and helpline / contact information — only on topics whose information has already been checked.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How information is checked</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Every guide is written by matching it against the information on the official portal <strong>edistrict.up.gov.in</strong>.</li>
        <li>Fees, timelines and rules are taken from that official source. A topic whose checking is still pending is NOT published until the check is complete.</li>
        <li>Where direct confirmation from the official portal is not possible, we publish only information already checked, and we state the source clearly.</li>
        <li>Government rules change from time to time. Every page shows its last-updated date so you can see how fresh the information is. Before applying, always check the fee and rules once on the official portal — the official portal's information is the one that counts.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>What we do not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No application is accepted or processed on this website.</strong> Applications happen only on the official portal edistrict.up.gov.in (eSathi login) or at an authorised CSC centre.</li>
        <li>We cannot see your application, tell you its status, or issue any certificate.</li>
        <li>We never ask for your <strong>eSathi login ID, password, OTP, or Aadhaar-linked information</strong> — not on this website, and not by email.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Corrections policy</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>If you find an error, outdated or wrong information in any guide, tell us via the Contact page or at <strong>edistrictupseva@gmail.com</strong>.</li>
        <li>We check the information, correct it, and update the page's last-updated date.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Author</h2>
      <p>Author of this site: <strong>Anwar Fakhri</strong>. The author's introduction is on the <a href="/en/about-us/">About Us</a> page.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
